WEBVTT

00:26:56.079 --> 00:27:00.496
The reactions were were vast, but it was
also something that was, you know,

00:27:01.163 --> 00:27:03.204
in various moments felt like
it was the right move.

00:27:03.579 --> 00:27:05.829
I imagine that happens a lot to that.

00:27:05.829 --> 00:27:09.996
You you rethink a classic world or story,

00:27:09.996 --> 00:27:13.788
whether it's Star Wars or Star Trek or
even characters that we've fallen in

00:27:13.788 --> 00:27:17.579
love with. Right. I still feel like,
you know, with Lost in particular,

00:27:17.579 --> 00:27:18.913
I still feel like, you know,

00:27:18.913 --> 00:27:23.038
Sawyer and Sayid and Kate and some of
the others are long lost friends.

00:27:23.496 --> 00:27:28.121
How often do you rethink the stories
you've told versus once you put it out

00:27:28.121 --> 00:27:31.413
into the world, you're you're happy with
the creative choices you've made,